  "lineage": "Polish góralski Tatra-Mountain highlander music-and-dance tradition of the Podhale region in southern Poland, performed by the Polish góral mountain-folk community. The kapela góralska ensemble centers on the prymista (lead violinist) accompanied by sekund (second-violin) and basy (three-string Tatra-style upright-bass), with characteristic open-string drone-and-shifted-tonal-center modal vocabulary distinct from broader Polish lowland folk-music. Performance contexts span village-festival celebrations, wedding ceremonies, and (since 1968) the international Folk-Music Festival in Zakopane. The post-1980 Tatra-cultural-revival under the local Highlander Union has consolidated institutional preservation. Distinguished from Slovak fujara solo and Czech moravian folk by Polish góralski Podhale-Tatra specific stylistic-conventions.",
